parents searching for answers this  morning after they say they were  notified that their kids were high on  marijuana edibles at school this  happened friday over at quest prep  academy near craig and rancho houston  spoke with one of those parents who says  there needs to be better emergency  protocols  i'm very upset i'm angry jenae simmelton  says her daughter ate an edible but was  not told until after that it contained  marijuana simpleton says this happened  in the morning and parents didn't know  until they tried to pick up their kids  there were probably  maybe four other parents there waiting  for the same reasons  they're not letting us see our kids talk  to them and have them call it all day  simpleton says kids were asleep on the  ground crying and one throwing up  indicating paramedics should have been  called simultan says she tried to speak  to the principal but was told she was  not available due to a holiday party she  says they did communicate hours later  but says more needs to be done knowing  that multiple kids were involved in  taking these edibles whether they were  their fault or not knowing or not once  you realize as an adult and as a parent  possibly  you should seek medical attention  simultan plans to contact the state  public charter school authority which  oversees quest academy saying stricter  safety measures need to be in place we  have to be the voices for our kids  whether they're right or wrong  the leadership at the school  failed us and failed them kate houston  live local now  we reached out to quest prep academy as  well as the state public charter school  authority asking for more information on  their drug safety protocols we haven't  heard back yet
 

